Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Preliminary functions and definitions", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.816434150172364*^9, 
  3.81643415749121*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"debede45-adeb-449c-b3b4-\
00b04bfc0b30"],

Cell["References", "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9346368454722557`*^9, 
  3.934636846728309*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5ba2155e-ea12-442a-a12f-\
e2878f00fc05"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "[1] sarah belcastro and Thomas C Hull. ",
 StyleBox["Modelling the folding of paper into three dimensions using affine \
transformations",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Linear Algebra and its applications, 348(1-3):273\[Dash]282, 2002.\n[2] \
Riccardo Foschi, Thomas C Hull, and Jason S Ku. ",
 StyleBox["Explicit kinematic equations for degree-4 rigid origami vertices, \
euclidean and non-euclidean",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Physical Review E, 106(5):055001, 2022.\n[3] Johnna Farnham, Thomas C \
Hull, and Aubrey Rumbolt. ",
 StyleBox["Rigid folding equations of degree-6 origami vertices",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Proceedings of the Royal Society A, 478(2260):20220051, 2022.\n[4] Fan \
Feng, Xiangxin Dang, Richard D. James, and Paul Plucinsky. ",
 StyleBox["The designs and deforma\.02tions of rigidly and flat-foldable \
origami",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Journal of the Mechanics and Physics of Solids, page 104018, 2020.\n[5] \
Fan Feng, Paul Plucinsky, and Richard D James. ",
 StyleBox["Helical miura origami",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Physical Review E, 101(3):033002, 2020.\n[6] Huan Liu, Paul Plucinsky, \
Fan Feng, and Richard D James. ",
 StyleBox["Origami and materials science",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society A, 379(2201):20200113, \
2021.\n[7] Matthew Grasinger, Andrew Gillman, and Philip Buskohl. ",
 StyleBox["Lagrangian approach to origami vertex analysis: Kinematics",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". arXiv preprint arXiv:2408.15460, 2024.\n[8] Hao Zhou, Matthew Grasinger, \
Philip Buskohl, and Kaushik Bhattacharya. ",
 StyleBox["Low energy fold paths in multistable origami structures",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". International Journal of Solids and Structures 265 (2023): 112125.\n[9] \
Tomas Moller and Ben Trumbore. ",
 StyleBox["Fast, minimum storage ray/triangle intersection",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". In ACM SIGGRAPH 2005 Courses, pages 7\[Dash]es. 2005.\n[10] Matthew \
Grasinger, Andrew Gillman, and Philip R. Buskohl. ",
 StyleBox["Multistability, symmetry and geometric conservation in eightfold \
waterbomb origami",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Proceedings of the Royal Society A 478, no. 2268 (2022): 20220270."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.934636851230576*^9, 3.934636852107128*^9}, {
   3.934636922073386*^9, 3.934636929065462*^9}, {3.9346369613311353`*^9, 
   3.9346370223317647`*^9}, {3.93463707519112*^9, 3.934637101527548*^9}, {
   3.9346371706251593`*^9, 3.9346371721138997`*^9}, {3.9346372155846815`*^9, 
   3.934637250019842*^9}, {3.9346374589307547`*^9, 3.9346374794782047`*^9}, {
   3.9346375279809203`*^9, 3.9346375387429304`*^9}, {3.93463863083216*^9, 
   3.934638662562226*^9}, 3.934638745896537*^9, {3.934644153794795*^9, 
   3.934644155773594*^9}, {3.9347515279092474`*^9, 3.9347515442869587`*^9}, {
   3.9347532602386503`*^9, 3.9347532777644725`*^9}, 
   3.934889279651647*^9},ExpressionUUID->"0ecc0f75-2c46-4ec4-8d8a-\
6172cb363c53"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Isometric mappings", "Subtitle",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.816434657412374*^9, 
  3.816434663327572*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ebc52112-5885-4a7f-b7ea-\
2b08071e4f35"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Consider an origami vertex where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0a5a8ea7-0dc2-4c44-81f6-e4e23d47baee"],
 " creases meet. Start at any crease, label it ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4e948c55-9291-4683-b378-7644d2243544"],
 ", and then proceed around the vertex in the counterclockwise direction, \
labeling each subsequent crease ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"2", ",", "3", ",", "...", ","}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "2,3,...,", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7ca35424-becc-463f-a706-ad82145eabe5"],
 " etc. Folding a crease in an origami involves the (relative) rotation of \
its adjacent faces by some angle, often called the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]fold angle\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and denoted by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|
    "boxes" -> FormBox["\[Phi]", TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\phi", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "21672da6-dda5-4de9-b0c1-56c4d0779aff"],
 ". As such, proper orthogonal linear transformations, and their associated \
matrix representations, are powerful tools for modeling the deformed state of \
an origami [1-7]. To this end, let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["r", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "A_r", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "680d041c-67d5-4a24-bb36-e72cd531076e"],
 " be the skew symmetric matrix associated with the cross product with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "r", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bd68af90-aa61-4916-9847-f499db4522ca"],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9346323387424736`*^9, 3.9346323551282544`*^9}, {
  3.9346324672195415`*^9, 3.934632541881525*^9}, {3.9346341987011924`*^9, 
  3.9346343070925107`*^9}, {3.9346344226704664`*^9, 3.934634450553598*^9}, {
  3.934634489785647*^9, 3.934634525673877*^9}, {3.9346345610447617`*^9, 
  3.9346347134514265`*^9}, {3.9346347800974417`*^9, 3.934634780379131*^9}, {
  3.9346351553697233`*^9, 3.9346352497355404`*^9}, {3.9346352850126495`*^9, 
  3.934635348150287*^9}, {3.934637612563758*^9, 3.9346376165993204`*^9}, {
  3.9348901233632317`*^9, 
  3.9348901250822706`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bf180621-e927-4476-a85b-\
bab5f5ecc1fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MatrixProduct", "[", "As_", "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"ret", ",", "i"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
      RowBox[{"take", " ", "a", " ", "product", " ", "of", " ", "matrices"}], 
      " ", "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ret", "=", 
       RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], ";", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"For", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"i", "=", "1"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[LessEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "As", "]"}]}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"i", "++"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ret", "=", 
          RowBox[{"ret", ".", 
           RowBox[{"As", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], 
       "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "ret"}]}], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.8310796253877707`*^9, {3.9346254869096727`*^9, 3.9346254917362747`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b6cd0a5b-e1bf-4968-a31b-f9b1b1c20dd2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"A", "[", "r_", "]"}], ":=", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"r", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"r", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"r", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "0", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"r", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"r", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"r", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "skew", " ", "symmetric", " ", "matrix", " ", "associated", " ", "with", " ",
     "cross", " ", "product", " ", "with", " ", "r"}], " ", "*)"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellChangeTimes->{{3.93462516059807*^9, 3.9346251789954505`*^9}, {
  3.934635293357798*^9, 3.9346352936285863`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"59991f6b-90e2-47b1-b016-0af2e21cb88b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Then a matrix representation of the rotation about a unit vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["r", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "r", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "680ff4b2-a779-4269-8a73-469b3b0718ff"],
 " by angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|
    "boxes" -> FormBox["\[Theta]", TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\theta", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7a87ac13-bf3e-4d76-870c-00e2ae20aa00"],
 " is given by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["r", "TI"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", "\[Theta]", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "exp", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"\[Theta]", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", "-", "cos", "\[Theta]"}], ")"}], 
         StyleBox["r", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
         StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "cos", "\[Theta]", 
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "+", "sin", "\[Theta]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["r", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "Q_r(\\theta)=\\exp(\\theta A_r)=(1-\\cos\\theta)r \\otimes r + \
\\cos\\theta I + \\sin\\theta A_r", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b3593a81-10e4-4a08-adb6-6e88a6f06beb"],
 ".",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[" ", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bd432483-e7b8-4dcc-97dd-6d0206a5a989"]
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9346353586496887`*^9, 3.9346353873344345`*^9}, {
   3.934635442915321*^9, 3.9346354782391768`*^9}, {3.934635532499363*^9, 
   3.934635566790028*^9}, 
   3.934635625655128*^9},ExpressionUUID->"eb98e163-d2cd-4421-be78-\
9086775b66f1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Q", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rvec_", ",", "\[Theta]_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", "-", 
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}]}], ")"}], "*", 
      RowBox[{"rvec", "\[TensorProduct]", "rvec"}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "*", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "*", 
      RowBox[{"A", "[", "rvec", "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], " ", 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "rotation", " ", "matrix", " ", "for", " ", "rotation", " ", "of", " ", 
    "angle", " ", "\[Theta]", " ", "about", " ", "the", " ", "rotation", " ", 
    "axis", " ", "r"}], " ", "*)"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.816434555663805*^9, {3.934625182361379*^9, 3.9346252137543936`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4bdd6f4f-7265-4a63-be07-aac0fb09ca44"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"transX", "[", 
    RowBox[{"points_", ",", "c_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x", "=", "points"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "translate", " ", "a", " ", "collection", " ", "of", " ", "points"}], 
      " ", "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"For", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"i", "=", "1"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[LessEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "x", "]"}]}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"i", "++"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"x", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], "=", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"x", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}], "+", "c"}]}], ";"}]}], 
       "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "x"}]}], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.816434159702943*^9, 3.816434160668063*^9}, {
  3.816434562789445*^9, 3.816434575740144*^9}, {3.9346252158969913`*^9, 
  3.934625225395173*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9575726b-f78d-4d4a-a187-db3da4b6afc7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rotatePts", "[", 
    RowBox[{"X_", ",", "QQ_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"Y", ",", "i"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "rotate", " ", "a", " ", "collection", " ", "of", " ", "points"}], " ", 
      "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Y", "=", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"For", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"i", "=", "1"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"i", "\[LessEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "X", "]"}]}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"i", "++"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Y", "=", 
          RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Y", ",", 
            RowBox[{"QQ", ".", 
             RowBox[{"X", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], 
       "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "Y"}]}], 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.8164346194277287`*^9, {3.9346253115563374`*^9, 3.9346253183247366`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c9efe895-38e8-4c0d-af48-1b5a78c87a7f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Generally, we are only interested in deformations of the origami up to full \
body rigid rotations and translations (of the entire structure). Therefore, \
we can fix the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]frame\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], so to \
speak, relative to full body rotations and translations, as convenient for \
simplifying derivations and computations. A standard convention is to assume \
that face 1 is fixed. Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "b_i", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0fc56bd3-f707-4f09-b43a-59b218bb6912"],
 " denote the unit vector along crease ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "i", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a7f24b70-19bd-45e6-a361-b9fe64eb759b"],
 " and oriented such that it is pointing away from the vertex. Then face 2 is \
mapped into the deformed configuration by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], "1"]], "(", 
         SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "1"], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {},
      "input" -> "Q_{b_1}(\\phi_1)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1a79bc73-b665-4d0f-a60d-3474f30e87cb"],
 "; that is, by rotating face 2 about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["b", "TI"], "1"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "b_1", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dc1c51bd-c92a-453c-bf87-46b77d7ec798"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "1"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\phi_1", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a7843b13-b118-43f6-946d-827df7c4e66c"],
 ". Face 3 is mapped into the deformed configuration by first rotating it \
relative to crease 2 and then, because it is attached to face 2, by crease 1 \
as well. Formally, face 3 is mapped by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], "1"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "1"], ")"}], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], "2"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "2"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "Q_{b_1}(\\phi_1)Q_{b_2}(\\phi_2)", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2ad2c56b-c57e-4607-b0cd-8e79bfbd3680"],
 ", face 4 by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], "1"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "1"], ")"}], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], "2"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "2"], ")"}], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], "3"]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "3"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "Q_{b_1}(\\phi_1)Q_{b_2}(\\phi_2)Q_{b_3}(\\phi_3)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8a3ad1b2-c1aa-44be-8d2f-09694bd8c3f7"],
 ", etc. For our choices of fold angles to be consistent with the assumption \
that face 1 is fixed, we require that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         UnderoverscriptBox["\[Product]", 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "1"}], 
          StyleBox["N", "TI"], LimitsPositioning -> True], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "1"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\prod_{i=1}^N Q_{b_i}(\\phi_1)=I", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "25cc41d5-a995-439f-bb34-1ccb07a88bfa"],
 " [1]. This is sometimes called the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]compatibility \
condition\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] [4,6,7] because it is required for the \
origami vertex to be able to be folded with the given fold angles and without \
tearing. (It also goes by the name \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]loop-closure \
condition\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] [1,7,8].) The below functions are used to \
compute folded deformation maps, and visualize folded origami \
configurations."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.934635702541665*^9, 3.934635721551777*^9}, {
  3.934636239240815*^9, 3.934636306082395*^9}, {3.934636390663862*^9, 
  3.934636399090137*^9}, {3.9346365147976794`*^9, 3.934636735380009*^9}, {
